From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: cdns-dphy: diagnostic override of the calibration wait time

Diagnostic only, inert by default. The kernel parameter
cdns_dphy.cal_wait_time=N, with N in 0..255, forces the
DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME field when the TX state machine is started.
The default, -1, keeps the value read from the register, which is the
behaviour introduced by 0017.

On Astrial H15 the first power on of the PHY after reset waits for the
lanes 320 us with the reset value 20, and 262 ms when the field is 0,
which is what the driver wrote before 0017. The build before 0017 showed
an image at boot and this one does not. Booting with cal_wait_time=0 is
the positive control: it reproduces the old behaviour without reverting
anything.

No log line on purpose: a printk on the 115200 serial console costs about
8 ms and would move the timing being measured. The value in use is in
/sys/module/cdns_dphy/parameters/cal_wait_time.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic, to be removed]

---
--- a/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/cadence/cdns-dphy.c
@@ -313,6 +313,10 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int cal_wait_time = -1;
+module_param(cal_wait_time, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cal_wait_time, "Diagnostic: force DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME to 0..255 at power on, -1 keeps it");
+
 static int cdns_dphy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 {
 	struct cdns_dphy *dphy = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
@@ -336,9 +340,10 @@
 	}
 
 	/* Start TX state machine. */
-	reg = readl(dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
-	writel((reg & DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME) | DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN | DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN,
-	       dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
+	reg = readl(dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM) & DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME;
+	if (cal_wait_time >= 0 && cal_wait_time <= 255)
+		reg = FIELD_PREP(DPHY_CMN_SSM_CAL_WAIT_TIME, cal_wait_time);
+	writel(reg | DPHY_CMN_SSM_EN | DPHY_CMN_TX_MODE_EN, dphy->regs + DPHY_CMN_SSM);
 
 	dphy->is_powered = true;
 	return 0;
